      "id": "54h8xgl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PHYSICAL QUANTITY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fundamental quantities (Mass, Length, Time, Temperature, Electric Current, Luminous Intensity, Amount of Substance) are independent of other physical quantities.",
        "Derived quantities such as velocity, acceleration, force, and density are expressed in terms of fundamental quantities.",
        "The SI system consists of 7 base units and 2 supplementary units (Radian for plane angle and Steradian for solid angle).",
        "Dimensional formulas represent physical quantities in terms of basic dimensions [M], [L], and [T].",
        "Density is defined as mass per unit volume and has the SI unit kg/m³."
      ],
      "id": "ykhs9wv"
    },
